        "knowledge_point": "Finding the Distribution of a Transformed Random Variable",
        "problem": "The random variable $X$ has the following probability distribution.\n\n| $x$ | $-0.5$ | $-0.25$ | $0$ | $0.25$ | $0.5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f_X(x)$ | $0.25$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ | $0.3$ |\n\nLet $Y=2-4X.$ The distribution of $Y$ is given below.\n\n| $y$ | $a$ | $3$ | $c$ | $1$ | $0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f_Y(y)$ | $0.25$ | $b$ | $0.1$ | $d$ | $0.3$ |\n\nWhat is the value of $a+b+c?$",
        "worked_solution": "First, let's add a $Y = 2-4X$ row to our table.\n\n| $x$ | $-0.5$ | $-0.25$ | $0$ | $0.25$ | $0.5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $4$ | $3$ | $2$ | $1$ | $0$ |\n| $f_X(x)$ | $0.25$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ | $0.3$ |\n\nNow, $f_X(x) = f_Y(y)$ for corresponding values of $X$ and $Y.$ Therefore, the distribution of $Y$ is as follows:\n\n| $y$ | $4$ | $3$ | $2$ | $1$ | $0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f_Y(y)$ | $0.25$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ | $0.3$ |\n\nSo, we have $a=4, b=0.2, c=2,$ and therefore $a+b+c =6.2.$",
